# urllib3 2.7.0 is not a dependency of ours — it is the copy pip vendors for
# itself. pip 26.2.1's vendor.txt records exactly "urllib3==2.7.0", and Trivy
# reports vendored packages. Verified against the published image: the only
# real urllib3 is 2.8.0 at
# usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/urllib3-2.8.0.dist-info, and there is
# no urllib3-2.7.0 dist-info in any layer. The server's HTTP traffic goes
# through requests -> that real 2.8.0; the vendored copy is only reachable by
# running pip, which this image never does at runtime.
#
# Not fixable by upgrading pip: 26.2.1 is the latest release and vendors
# urllib3 2.7.0. Our own floor is enforced in pyproject.toml (urllib3>=2.8.0).
# A multi-stage build that strips pip would also clear it, but saves only a
# few MB and complicates the Dockerfile, so it is not worth it.
# https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97687
# https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-97689
# Re-evaluate on the next pip release. Target removal: 2026-12-31.
CVE-2026-97687
CVE-2026-97689
